id: pm-gd6vnn
title: "Observation contract: a declared, versioned observation whose guaranteed ceiling and workspace-calibrated expected cost are both readable before the call, so a training run is plannable"
description: "Third of the four seams pm-klxax7 owns, and the epic states its resolution rule: this is pm-5t33or's contract-declared budgets viewed from the environment side, and the two must resolve to one mechanism rather than two. A command budget is an egress ceiling, which is what an interactive agent needs. A training run planning ten thousand episodes needs the cost while planning, not while stepping, and a 4,000-token ceiling on a call that typically returns 300 is a correct ceiling and a useless plan. So an observation must publish both numbers without being performed: the guaranteed ceiling derived from constituent command budgets, and a calibrated expectation measured from emitted bytes against the workspace actually in use. Duplicate check: searched observation/budget/bounded-read lineages and read pm-5t33or, pm-cxr0jb, pm-hb7ug8, pm-t5dt4z, pm-8bgeye, pm-tch9cs; none publishes a pre-call calibrated expectation for a named observation."
type: Feature
