acceptance_criteria: "An observation is a named versioned selection over read surfaces declared as data; its ceiling and calibrated expectation are readable without performing it; calibration input is emitted bytes rather than a bytes-per-token constant; each observation declares whether its cost is corpus-independent or corpus-dependent and the declaration holds at the 10k, 100k and 1M fixtures; degradation follows a declared ladder and the served tier is reported to the caller; the same declaration against a seeded workspace is byte-identical across processes and machines"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make observation cost knowable before the call so long environment runs can be budgeted deterministically
value: A training or evaluation run plans against published cost instead of overprovisioning against a ceiling or gambling on a typical case
why_now: pm-5t33or is in flight; resolving the environment-side requirement into it now avoids a second parallel budget mechanism
